  "static_conclusions": [
    "The separately allocated stable record is initialized before provider register. OPEN admits one FnMut, CLOSING is stored before external request, and busy protects callback/provider/environment cleanup reentry. Raw queued/pre-trampoline/rejected users keep the record alive until actual unsafe provider status1 no-future.",
    "Only status1 with no admitted callback destroys the environment once and sets CLOSED; Pending keeps record/Task obligation, other statuses trap without releasing, explicit finish requires CLOSED. Failed installation uses the synchronous no-future promise; OOM/install tests exercise real moved environment cleanup.",
    "Verify-derived intrusive owner records remain linked on Pending. Cancellation requests active child/pollable roots before draining, and normal/owned results retain explicit prepared-result responsibility. Source Await fixtures reach cleanup Pending before Ready.",
    "Both kernels establish legacy TaskI32 NoExternal at every actual TaskStart, including unused/unreachable instructions; actual calls, function/foreign-function refs, Closure entry and teardown are scanned. Unknown indirect/Dyn targets reject. TaskI32 is not granted arbitrary caller-derived worker permission.",
    "New Task<T> origins are reconstructed from actual TaskCreate/Start SSA and consuming sum/product/local transfers; unknown helper or parameter origins remain conservative. The TakeErrorUnion producer/consumer omission discovered during this review was corrected in both kernels, and exact synchronous source controls now pass.",
    "The independently implemented resource cleanup entry checks cover Direct owning local aggregates, selected partial fields and FnOnce consumption. General Task<T> Closure/Package source paths still stop at prior Types fences; they are not counted as reached new proof controls.",
    "Actual unique machine NamedType definitions determine layout and field identity. Missing/cyclic/deep definitions reject before layout/hash growth; opaque pointers do not invent pointee layout. ABI cache identity binds actual named fields and compiler/runtime options."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "No formal full workspace gate, merge/main acceptance, complete G8.4, cross-thread wakeup, general scheduler, borrowed frame-port or general owning Sum claim.",
